 to the last full rebuild's timestamp, never the last\ncontinuous run's, even though that timestamp is tracked and already used\ncorrectly for the \"is there anything new\" check. On Doris this meant every\ncontinuous run reprocessed everything changed since the last full rebuild\nrather than just since the last continuous run, with cost growing\nunboundedly between full rebuilds - confirmed live: a single-row mutation\ntriggered a ~3.5 minute run, matching a ~96,000-row mutation's cost.\n\nScoped the fix to sqlBuilder.requiresUniqueKeyAnalyticsTables() (true only\nfor Doris) rather than the shared code path, since Postgres's \"latest\"\npartition is wholesale-replaced on every continuous run (not merged), so\nnarrowing its window would silently discard previously-captured\nincremental data. Doris merges into the persistent main table with\nnatural-key deduplication, so a narrower window is safe there. Verified\nzero behavior change for Postgres (existing tests, unchanged, still pass).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","author":{"name":"Jason Pickering","email":"jason@dhis2.org"},"id":"c35bace50f8407d80f2807987df13193cba69c51","tree_id":"863558f453ec2fad86e4502717e247a81076ff71","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:15:25Z","committer":{"name":"Jason Pickering","email":"jason@dhis2.org"}},"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/workflows/10954","repository":{"id":66940520,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk2Njk0MDUyMA==","owner":{"login":"dhis2","id":1089987,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjEwODk5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1089987?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2","gravatar_id":"","type":"Organization","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhis2/followers","gists_url